","alias":"constructionendyear"},{"name":"cost","type":"esriFieldTypeDouble","alias":"cost"},{"name":"dedicationdate","type":"esriFieldTypeString","alias":"dedicationdate","length":50},{"name":"dedicationinfo","type":"esriFieldTypeString","alias":"dedicationinfo","length":1000},{"name":"presidentatconstruction","type":"esriFieldTypeString","alias":"presidentatconstruction","length":50},{"name":"squarefootage","type":"esriFieldTypeInteger","alias":"squarefootage"}],"features":[{"attributes":{"OBJECTID":315,"ABBR":"CREC","Name":"France A. Córdova Recreational Sports Center","OTHER_ABBR":"RSC","OWNER":"PURDUE","ADDRESS":"355 N. Martin Jischke Drive","BUILTYear":1325462400000,"OCCUPIEDYear":null,"RazeYear":253402214399000,"Shape.STArea()":24564.792858745001,"Shape.STLength()":840.11915442757584,"description":"A multi-phase addition and renovation to the Recreational Gymnasium was completed in 2012. The addition was needed to move Purdue's recreational facilities closer to other Big Ten schools' standards. This addition included enhancing cardiovascular fitness space, free weight, indoor jogging/walking, group exercise/multipurpose space, and basketball courts. There was also upgrades to the racquetball courts, gym space and venues, and additional spaces for locker rooms, wellness space, free zone/common space, and food and dining areas. Besides adding space and equipment, the expansion added new concepts to the gymnasium. These new concepts included connecting the east and west entrances with an atrium that is open to everyone and offers healthy snacks and accessible health and wellness services. During the renovation, it was renamed the France A. Córdova Recreational Sports Center. It is affectionately known on campus as the Co-Rec.","buildingidlong":168,"ChangeYear":1514764800000,"constructionbeginyear":2008,"constructionendyear":2012,"cost":98000000.0,"dedicationdate":"2012-10-12","dedicationinfo":"The building is named after past Purdue President France A. Córdova. 